cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these materials, please cite them as below."
type: software
title: "ME 50900 – Intermediate Fluid Mechanics at Purdue University: Jupyter notebooks"
abstract: >-
  Jupyter notebooks for ME 50900, Intermediate Fluid Mechanics, at Purdue
  University. The notebooks cover tensors, kinematics, unidirectional flows,
  the Navier–Stokes equations, ideal flow, dimensional analysis, similarity
  solutions, boundary layers, Stokes flow, and lubrication theory, using
  Python with SymPy for symbolic calculations and Matplotlib for
  visualizations. Each notebook opens in Google Colab with nothing to install.
